    <!--
      0.27.0 (draft), Phase 1017 rides it - additive. A connector declares
      whether it takes a credential (`CredentialNeed`: `NoCredential` /
      `Required` / `Optional`, through `IDeclaresCredentialNeed`), and the
      `DataIngestor` reads the secret store only when it does: a NONE
      connector is never asked, and a REQUIRED one with no secret fails as
      `CredentialMissing` before `Connect`. Undeclared reads as `Optional`,
      the previous behaviour. The CSV, Excel, Parquet and in-memory sources
      declare NONE, so file ingest no longer depends on the secret store;
      every other shipped connector declares OPTIONAL with its reason.
      Additive: `CredentialNeed`, `IDeclaresCredentialNeed`,
      `CredentialNeed.declaredBy` (Platform.Server);
      `Credentials.resolveDeclared` (DataSources.Common).
      Migration recipe: `docs/migrations/1017-connector-credential-need.md`.
