      Phase 1060 rides the 0.38.0 draft (untagged, publicly unpinned; its
      surface movement is additive, below the draft's class):
      `ToolUp.Platform.Core` gains `ScopeKey`, `PlatformShard`,
      `ScopePersistence`, `AuditScope` and `StorageScope.ofKey`;
      `ToolUp.Platform.Server` gains
      `StorageScopeDerivation.tryKeyFromSubject`. Nothing is removed or
      retyped.
      Phase 1089 rides the 0.38.0 draft, breaking: every fact id moves onto `CanonicalFrame.digest` (persisted ids migrate once through `BlobFactStore.MigrateIds` / `FactStoreMigration.migrateIds`), and `CountersignatureCanonical.sha256Hex` gives way to `Sha256.hex` / `Sha256.hexOfUtf8`. Migration recipe: `docs/migrations/1089-redesign-h-sha256-hex-and-canonicalframe.md`.
    -->
    <!--
      Phase 1052 rides the 0.38.0 draft (untagged, publicly unpinned; the
      draft is already breaking, and so is this: `ServerApp` gains
      `Contributions`, so a full record literal adds a field - build from
      `ServerApp.empty`). `ToolUp.Platform.Server` gains `ServiceConfig.append`,
      `Contribution` / `ContributionKind` / `Contribution.service`,
      `ServerApp.addContribution`, `ServerApp.addServiceConfig` and
      `ServerApp.serviceConfig`. Companions now contribute their DI
      registrations to `Contributions` instead of folding them into
      `Extensions.ServiceConfig`, so code that read that field to build a
      provider reads `ServerApp.serviceConfig app`. Migration recipe:
      `docs/migrations/1052-serviceconfig-append-and-contribution-service.md`.
      Phase 860 rides the 0.38.0 draft (untagged, publicly unpinned; its
      surface movement is breaking-class, the draft's own class, not above
      it): `ToolUp.Platform.Server`'s `CompositionManifest` gains
      `LiveInterfaceTools`, so a full record construction adds a field (the
      in-tree constructions are `CompositionManifest.build` and the `with*`
      builders, which callers use). The rest is additive:
      `CompositionManifest.isLiveInterfaceTool` / `liveInterfaceToolsOf` /
      `liveInterfaceTools` / `recordsLiveInterfaceTools` /
      `withLiveInterfaceTools`, `LiveInterfaceSchemaVersion`, and
      `DeploymentReadinessReport.liveInterfaceFromManifest` /
      `registerManifestLiveInterface`. `SchemaVersion` steps to 3; the field
      is not sealed, and a composition seals to the same bytes as before.
    -->
    <!-- Phase 1066 rides the 0.38.0 draft, breaking: `IJobScheduler.Schedule` answers `ScheduleOutcome` (`Scheduled` / `Coalesced`) and `TriggerOnce` refuses with `TriggerError`; codemod rules `1066-*`, migration recipe `docs/migrations/1066-redesign-d-schedulerpolicy-coalesced-and-joblifecycle-transition.md`. -->
    <!--
      Phase 1150 rides the 0.38.0 draft (untagged, publicly unpinned; the
      draft is already breaking): `FactTableDetail` and `FactTableColumnView`
      gain `Description: string option`, and `ServerModule` / `ServerApp`
      gain a description field each, so a full record literal adds a field
      (`Description = None`; build modules and apps from `create` / `empty`).
      Additive otherwise: `FactTableDescription`, `IDescribesFactTables`,
      `ServerModule.describeFactTables`, `ServerApp.factTableRegistry`,
      `FactTableRegistry.tryDescription`. Migration recipe:
      `docs/migrations/1150-fact-table-descriptions.md`.
