    <!-- Phase 1090 rides the 0.38.0 draft, breaking: the per-envelope job-payload serialisers, `tryParse*` and `isTerminal` give way to `JobPayload` and each handler module's `failureOf`, and the eight model/fact handler classes are gone (their modules keep `create` and the handler names); additive `SidecarStore<'T>`, `RunKind`, `RunJob<'Req>`, `RunFailure`, `ConditionalDataObjectStore.isAtomic`. Migration recipe, including the one rolling-upgrade step: `docs/migrations/1090-sidecarstore-and-runjob.md`. -->
    <!-- Phase 1135 rides the 0.38.0 draft, breaking: `StartupModes.StartupMode` gains `RunOperatorTask` (an exhaustive match adds the case), `ScopeMigrationReport` gains `Skipped` and `AuditId` (a full record literal adds both) and `ScopeMigrationOutcome` gains `WouldMigrate` (an exhaustive match adds the case); additive otherwise: the operator-task startup mode's seam (`StartupModes.OperatorTask`, `operatorTask`, `operatorTaskOut`), `FactStoreMigration.preview`, `FactsMigrateTask`, `FactStoreMigrationCompose.withFactsMigrateTask`, and the `toolup facts migrate` verb. -->
    <!--
      Phase 1151 rides the same draft: `ServerModule` and `ServerApp` gain a subject-description field each
      (`SubjectDescriptions` / `RegisteredSubjectDescriptions`; a full record literal adds it, or builds from
      `create` / `empty`). Additive otherwise: `SubjectDescription`, `IDescribesSubjects`,
      `ServerModule.describeSubjects`, `ServerApp.metricRegistry`, `MetricRegistry.buildDescribed`,
      `MetricRegistry.trySubjectDescription`. Recipe: `docs/migrations/1150-fact-table-descriptions.md`.
    -->
    <Version>0.38.0</Version>
    <!--
      The draft note is APPEND-ONLY. A change that rides or advances the
      <Version> above appends ONE line at the END of the list below the
      marker, and never edits or reorders a line already in it:

        - <phase> (<version it rides>): <class> — <one sentence>

      <class> is what the surface guard says the change is (breaking,
      additive, or none), and the sentence names what a consumer must know,
      with its migration note if there is one. Two branches that each append
      a line then merge without a hand resolution through the draftnote mode
      of dev-scripts/merge-baselines.ps1 (registered by
      the Setup target of Build.fsproj); a paragraph inserted above <Version>,
      the form the blocks before it use, conflicts with every concurrent
      change that does the same. Keep each line free of a double hyphen: it
      ends an XML comment. A release keeps the list; the version act that
      opens the next draft appends below it like any other line.
      ==== draft notes: append ONE line per change below this marker, never edit one ====
      - 1149 (0.38.0): none — CHANGELOG.md is rendered at release instead of by each change, this note is append-only, and the merge drivers are registered through the clone's common directory; no package surface moves (docs/migrations/1149-changelog-at-release.md).
      - 1094 (0.38.0): breaking — IModelFitProvider, IModelRegistry and IExternalComputeDispatcher gain an abstract Capabilities member (codemod rules 1094-*), IIsolatedComputeBackend and ModelFitWorkSpec.isArtifactDigest are removed, and a facts or model-execution composition that cannot be built raises CompositionRefused; additive ServiceComposition, DatasetStore.readAll, FactTool.define, the result builder and Hex64; recipe docs/migrations/1094-redesign-h-factscompose-options-modelling-dedup-and-fact-tools.md
      - 1091 (0.38.0): breaking — FactDraft, BatchAssertOutcome, BatchAssertReceipt, FactEvents and the three fact audit payloads move from ToolUp.Facts.Server to ToolUp.Facts.Core (same namespace, so source recompiles unchanged; a consumer compiled against 0.37.0 rebuilds); FactWrite.plan is the one write core both stores execute, FactAudit and FactCompetition the one audit writer and competition indicator, BlobFactStore.SurfaceFaults is added, and six DelegateMint draft and id constructors are removed for one internal DelegateMint.draft (docs/migrations/1091-redesign-h-factwrite-plan-and-one-store-scope.md).
      - 1156 (0.38.0): breaking — `BlockRender.BlockOutcome` (ToolUp.AI.Client) gains `Computed` (an exhaustive match adds the case); additive otherwise: `PresentationCompose.withPipelineTool` composes evaluate_pipeline in the answering form and mounts `IPipelineBlockApi`, and the panel draws a pipeline block re-run under the reader's gate (docs/migrations/1156-pipeline-tool-composed.md).
      - 1096 (0.38.0): additive — ToolUp.Platform.Build gains Gate (Exclusion, exclude, scannedDirs, solutionProjects, findings, reconcile: every *.Tests.fsproj is a VerifyAll pack or a named exclusion) and PackScope (the one declaration of the directories Pack and Publish never pack); BuildConfig and TestPack are unchanged, and nine baselines drop the band-dependent SerializationInfo constructor line, which the comparer already ignores.
      - 1093 (0.38.0): additive — the disclosure gate decides each fact in four pure stages (`DisclosureStages`) composed by `FactDisclosureGate.Read` into one `GroundedRead` per fact, `Check` its verdict projection; the taint stage walks a write-maintained `DisclosureTaintIndex` read through `IDisclosureTaintIndexSource` (BlobFactStore: one index blob per scope; PostgresFactStore: the `<table>_taint` table, created by AutoMigrate, to provision by hand under VerifyOnly) instead of listing the scope per check; `AnswerPlanProvenance.withPlans` is the one plan stitching of the answer chain and the certificate; where two facts produced one data-object version the taint walk now counts every producer upstream (fail-closed).
      - 1155 (0.38.0): additive — `ToolUp.Platform.Core` gains the optional `IAttributesDeclarations` capability (`MetricRegistry.tryRegistrations`), and `ToolUp.Facts.Server` gains `FactDeclarationsAudit`, `UndescribedDeclarations` and `FactDeclarationsValidator`: composing the fact store registers a preflight validator that logs, at Info, each metric without Context and each table or subject without a description, by module; it never refuses.
      - 1148 (0.38.0): additive — `StorageScope.tryKey`, `StorageScope.tryTeamId` and `ResolvedScope.Key` read the `ScopeKey` a scope renders from; every scope literal under src/ renders through `ScopeKey` and `VerifyScopeLiterals` is a zero with named exceptions; the swept readers use the strict parser, so an empty or padded id after a `team-` / `user-` prefix is no longer read as that scope (docs/migrations/1148-scope-literal-sweep.md).
      - 1152 (0.38.0): additive — `ToolUp.Facts.Server` gains `list_fact_tables` (`FactTablesTool`: the declared tables projected over the browse reads as a typed `FactTableView` list, each table's sampled facts judged at FactToolResult, a denied table named with its policy only, never a value), declared by `FactsCompose.withFactStore` beside the other fact tools through `NarrativeGrounding.factTools`, and `FactBrowseHandler.detailOf`; `list_metric_coverage`'s description points table-shaped questions at it.
      - 1141 (0.38.0): breaking — `AnswerVerifier.ScopedFact` (ToolUp.AI.Server) gains `Inputs` and `VerifiedNumber` (ToolUp.AI.Core) gains `DerivedFrom`, so a full record literal of either adds the field; additive otherwise: `ToolUp.Facts.Server` gains `aggregate_metric` (`AggregateMetricTool`, a total summed by the server from gated facts, only for a metric declared `Additive`) as the fifth of `NarrativeGrounding.factTools`, `ToolUp.Facts.Core` its types (`AggregateQuery`, `AggregateResult`, `AggregateRefusal` and their parts), and the numeric answer gate verifies figures from the turn's fact-tool results (`AnswerVerifier.toolResultFacts`, `runVerificationStageWithScope`) and a derived total against the facts it names (docs/migrations/1141-aggregate-metric-tool.md).
      - 1154 (0.38.0): additive — `ToolUp.Facts.Server` gains `FactTablesOptions` (`MemberCap`, default 20, 0 turns it off; declared with `FactsCompose.withFactTablesOptions`), `FactLevelMembers` (`Listed` names and a count of the rest, or `CountOnly`), the `Members` field on `FactTableLevelView` and `FactTablesTool.projectWith` / `executeWithOptions` / `executeFor`: the level a table rows sit at names its members in `list_fact_tables` when it holds at most the cap, each name read through the FactToolResult gate, the withheld counted and never named, a level above the cap reporting its count only (a full record literal of `FactTableLevelView` gains `Members`).
      - 1142 (0.38.0): breaking — `PopulationQuery` gains `PathAnyOf` and `PathExclude` (a full record literal adds both, FS0764; the `create` form is unchanged), applied by every store in the subject predicate before ranking and the statistics; additive `PopulationQuery.pathStartsWith`, `PopulationQuery.asOnePrefix` and `OnePrefixPath`, through which the delegated store translates the filters or refuses one by name; `query_metric_population` takes `path_any_of` and `path_exclude` and echoes its `filters` (docs/migrations/1142-population-path-filters.md).
      - 1146 (0.38.0): breaking — `PipelineRefusal` (ToolUp.Facts.Core) gains fourteen cases, the assertion's refusals (an exhaustive match adds them); additive otherwise: `PresentationCompose.withDerivedAssertions` (ToolUp.Facts.Presentation.Server) lets evaluate_pipeline assert a result column as `Computed` facts of a registered derived metric through `PipelineAssertion` (ToolUp.Facts.Server), each naming its input facts as `fact:<id>` (`FactInput`), and the taint walk reads those as a computed lineage (docs/migrations/1146-pipeline-assertion.md).
      - 1144 (0.38.0): additive — `ToolUp.Facts.Core` gains `FactRendering.renderFor` and `CurrencySymbols` (`table`, `tryFind`, `prefix`), and every fact-rendering door renders through `renderFor`: a metric declared `currency` with an ISO 4217 `Unit` and a `C` format renders with its currency's symbol (`£21,240` where it rendered `¤21,240`), from a table rather than culture data, an unknown code as its own prefix (`CHF 1,299`); every other metric and `render` itself are unchanged. A visible change: a consumer that worked around `¤` with a custom format can return to `C0` / `C2` (docs/migrations/1144-currency-from-the-metric-unit.md).
      - 1092 (0.38.0): breaking — `FactTableRunRecord` (ToolUp.Platform.Core) gains `Options : RunOptions` and `RecordVersion`, so a full record literal adds both (build one with `FactTableRun.opened`); a run's options ride its record, so `OpenRun`, `Runs` and `Status` return them, and a record written before reads `RunOptions.empty`; `FactTableRun` gains the pure lifecycle (`opened`, `tryOpen`, `stage`, `commit`, `reject`, `abandon`, `hasEnded`, `statusName`) over the new `OpenFactTableRun` that both writers execute; additive `RunOptions` / `RunSlice` / `RunMethod`, `FactTableRunOptions.toRun` / `ofRun`, `FactTableWriteError.ofTransition`; the delegated writer takes run inputs (a slice is still refused) and `DelegatedFactStore` reads the disclosure-taint index through its inner store (docs/migrations/1092-redesign-h-runrecord-facttablerun-and-the-recompute-path.md).
      - 1143 (0.38.0): additive — `query_metric_population` takes `with_metrics` (up to `PopulationQueryTool.MaxCompanionMetrics` registered ids, each refused by name if unregistered; with them `top_k` is at most `PopulationQueryTool.MaxCompanionTopK`): each ranked member that crossed the gate carries `companions`, point reads for its subject and period gated at FactToolResult one by one (a withheld one is a marker, a missing one `absent`), and an answer without companions is byte-identical to before (docs/platform/facts.md).
      - 1053 (0.38.0): breaking — caller-less members go from ToolUp.Platform.Server (ThreadSafeCell, Reader, ReaderBuilder, the Extensions module, Write.stackalloc, ParsingArgumentsError) and ToolUp.Platform.Core (Read.interpretIntegerAs, Write.Fable, moved to the Fable test tier); a [&lt;Custom&gt;] validator that cannot be built refuses at compose time; the in-memory stores share one bounded FIFO that never wipes; ToolUp.Platform.Build gains CodemodMigration.RemotingLeftovers (codemod rules 1053-*; docs/migrations/1053-redesign-b-defects-remoting.md)
      - 1157 (0.38.0): breaking — every IFactStore member takes a ResolvedScope and answers Result&lt;_, FactStoreError&gt; (the seven string overloads go, a storage fault on a read is StorageFault, never absence), and the string scope forms of the disclosure gate, clause planner, answer planner, fact resolver, evidence source, provenance graph, table writer, narrative ingestor and grounding seams are removed or retyped; carried jobs refuse a scope nobody re-minted, coherence sweeps resolve declared principals (codemod rules 1157-*; docs/migrations/1157-one-scope-form.md).
      - 1161 (0.38.0): breaking — the delegated writer takes a period slice (every stored delegated row names the run that wrote it, a carried row mints under its own run, and a slice over rows stored before attribution is refused until the facts-attribute-delegate-rows operator task records them), a delegated table, quote or lineage read that fails answers StorageFault rather than a refusal fact or a shorter answer, `FactsMigrateCommand.Options` gains `Task` (a full record literal adds it) and `IFactTableWriterContract.runOptionsRefusedTests` is removed; additive `RunRecord` / `RunProvenance` / `RunOutcome` over `ResolvedScope` with a `toRunRecord` projection of every stored run kind, `FactsOperatorTaskCompose.withFactsOperatorTasks` (facts-attribute-delegate-rows, facts-reissue-jobs, run by `toolup facts migrate` with its attribute-delegate-rows or reissue-jobs flag) and `IFactStoreContract.readFaultTests` (docs/migrations/1161-delegate-executor-completes.md).
      - 1165 (0.38.0): breaking — `TeamPermissions` (ToolUp.Platform.Core) gains `Pages` (a full record literal adds it, FS0764; a stored document without it reads as empty and writes back byte-identically) and `AuditEvent` gains `PageSaved`, `PageReseeded`, `PageDetached` and `PageWriteRefused` (an exhaustive match adds them); additive otherwise: ToolUp.Platform.Server gains the page store (`IPageDocumentStore`, `BlobPageDocumentStore`, `PageDocumentStoreCompose.withPageDocumentStore`) and the layer fold (`PageLayers`), and takes the published Fuaran op packages (docs/migrations/1165-page-store.md).
    -->
    <!--
      IsPackable defaults to true for SDK-style projects that produce a
      DLL. Non-publishable projects (App composition roots, modules,
      test packs, commercial-internal) opt out per-fsproj.
    -->
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <!--
      Phase 11.C.2 closure (2026-05-11) — packed-README default. Every
      packable SDK fsproj inherits <PackageReadmeFile>. Single-side
      companions where README.md is a sibling of the fsproj are auto-
      included via the <ItemGroup> below; cross-tier companions add
      an explicit per-fsproj <None Include="..\ToolUp.X\README.md"...>
      so all tiers share one parent README.
    -->
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!--
      Shared brand icon — single source of truth at repo-root icon.png.
      128x128 transparent PNG (NuGet's recommended display size). The
      packed <None Include> in the ItemGroup below ships the byte
      payload into every IsPackable nupkg; this property references it
      by filename so re-cutting the icon is one-file churn, not 48.
    -->
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Auto-include a sibling README.md for packable projects that have
    one. Cross-tier companions (where README.md lives in the parent
    docs directory, not next to the fsproj) add their own explicit
    <None Include="..\X\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' != 'false' And Exists('$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)\README.md')">
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Pack the shared brand icon into every IsPackable nupkg. <PackageIcon>
    in the PropertyGroup above references it by filename; this ItemGroup
    ships the byte payload from the single repo-root icon.png.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' != 'false'">
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!--
    Phase 804 (closing 69k.E) - the remoting generator's build integration,
    imported in-tree so the samples dogfood the very targets a consumer gets
    from the ToolUp.Remoting.Generator package (a PrivateAssets="all"
    reference; see src/ToolUp.Remoting.Generator/README.md). INERT for every
    project that declares no ToolUpRemotingDecoders / ToolUpRemotingDispatch
    item: each target's condition is then false and nothing runs, so a
    project that never opts in builds byte-for-byte as before. The tool is
    resolved at target time to the generator project's own build output,
    and a declaring project orders itself after it with a build-only
    ProjectReference (samples/HelloWorld-AOT/HelloWorld.AOT.Contract).
  -->
  <Import Project="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)src/ToolUp.Remoting.Generator/build/ToolUp.Remoting.Generator.targets"
          Condition="Exists('$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)src/ToolUp.Remoting.Generator/build/ToolUp.Remoting.Generator.targets')" />
</Project>
